Z||000000||Mattyman||09-29-2001||09:48 PM||||Today i went to the junkyard to get a headlight control module that i needed.  I called up a week before and the guy said that they had 3 87 Fieros. So i get there today and he tells me where they are and i look at them and im like these are all older than 87.  Hes like what do u mean and i told him i could tell by the style. He was like did u look at this sticker under the trunk that has the year on it and i told him i didnt have because i could tell.  So he went over and opened it up and was looking and then said, opps i guess this is an 84.  What an idiot. Good thing they had an 87 Fierbird so i got it out of that.  The one Fiero there was a notchback with the fiero emblem painted on the hood, and the ttops were still in tack on the car.  I might go back and pick them up since they are getting rare.  Finally i went home and ripped off the front drivers side fender and repaced the module.  And the lights now work.  Yessssss im happy again.||||reg||1
